    "The anchor refreshed the attacker's requested lines on all three pools, so each is a target. Each proxy ran its implementation from creation; initialize() later pointed it at its pool config and fee manager, whose getDueInfo supplies the elapsed period, so those pointer writes are the resets.",
    "Campaign: the attacker's drawdown, and a copycat that repeated request, refresh and drawdown against two further Huma v1 pools. No unapproved drawdown occurred on any of these pools before the anchor (DrawdownMade borrowers all had an earlier CreditApproved)."
